    "path": "architecture/storage-tiers.md",
    "title": "Storage Tiers",
    "score": 0.4873999025217278,
    "confidence": 0.52,
    "snippet": "Readings move through three tiers as they age. - Hot (7 days): columnar tables on SSD, serves the live dashboard. - Warm (90 days): compressed objects in bucket storage, queried on demand. - Cold (7 years): archival storage, restored only on request. After the hot window, raw readings are downsampled into 1-minute rollups before they move to warm. Deletion and holds are governed by the retention policy. Data arrives through the [[ingest-pipeline]].",
